{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Did not pour.</b> Did not reach — and even those that were in the air did not reach the ground. And similar to it: ״וַתִּתַּךְ עָלֵינוּ הָאָלָה וְהַשְּׁבוּעָה״ (Daniel 9) — of Ezra: and it reached upon us. And Menachem ben Seruk classified it in the section ״כְּהִתּוּךְ כֶּסֶף״ (Ezekiel 22) — a term of pouring molten metal, and I accept his words, as its Targum: וְיָצַק — וְאַתִּיךְ, לָצֶקֶת — לְאַתָּכָא. So too here, לֹא נִתַּךְ לָאָרֶץ — was not poured to the ground."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:18.736724520Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}